course: dictionary
lesson: 915
title: A French word in English
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Blanc is a French word. It means white, but on its own it is not an English word. You will meet it hidden inside English names and phrases, so use the words around it to work out what it means.
explain: «Mont Blanc» means White Mountain. It is the highest mountain in the Alps, and it sits on the border of France and Italy. The name itself gives you the clue: mont is a mountain, and blanc is white.
explain: Some phrases are harder. «Sauvignon blanc» is a white wine, and «carte blanche» means full freedom. In these phrases blanc is not about colour at all, so always check whether your meaning makes sense in the sentence.
fact: Blanc is the French word for white.
fact: «Mont Blanc» means White Mountain. It is the highest mountain in the Alps, at about 4,800 metres.
fact: «Sauvignon blanc» is a white wine, and «carte blanche» means full freedom.
fact: Blanc changes to match the noun it goes with: «un chat noir» and «une souris blanche» swap to «un chat blanc» and «une souris noire».
fact: The French flag is bleu, blanc, rouge: blue, white, red, in that order from the flagpole.
exercise: «Mont Blanc» is the name of a famous mountain. What does blanc mean in this name? | *White | Red | Black | Blue
exercise: The French flag is «bleu, blanc, rouge». Which colour is in the middle? | Blue | Green | Red | *White
exercise: In «un chat noir» and «une souris blanche», the colours swap. What is the new phrase for the mouse? | *une souris noire | une souris bleue | une souris blanche | un chat noir
test: What is «sauvignon blanc»? | A red flag | A white mountain | *A white wine
test: About how tall is Mont Blanc? | *4,800 metres | 48,000 metres | 480 metres
exam: What does «carte blanche» mean in English? | Being very quiet | *Full freedom | A white card for a sale | A sad feeling
